      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e2-twenty-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/eef95305-c811-50a4-9157-bfd4e5780c24/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:50b985f905842d1f3d17632b0c3cab77fa19edf026bb0dc1730d26f4bef07537). Two visually identical backpacks differ in presentation: one is highlighted and labelled Empfohlen while the other is neutral. Budget and intended hiking use are visible in the shopper thought, making a framing/salience question concrete without claiming a measured bias or an objectively superior product. At 360 px the identical alternatives, highlighted recommendation label, shopper and budget/use thought remain clear. Side slogans are decorative. At 680 px the same backpack features in both frames and the lack of additional product facts make the presentation difference recognizable. The shopper looks toward the presented alternatives; no directional document, instrument or notebook is being read. Actual targeted concept-clarification motif review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-08/wirtschaft-e2-bias-concept-clarification-native-preparation-20261008-v1/native-d-eef-single-final/round-a/independent-round-a-inspection.receipt.json (sha256:4b2e8f0cb1bf87c0df9075efb49866bd3221cde01bf4abef83a7c8ff3bb61564). The same asset was actually reviewed again at native/360/680 and on the fresh native page; KEEP remains justified for the clarified concept analysis. No image bytes, human approval or learner evidence changed."
