      "aiReviewer": "OpenAI Codex economics_visual_memory_audit",
      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e1-seventeen-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/c4c5bae8-575a-5a70-ba30-bada55f93abb/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:8da4dd5514d42c5a5fb083e6bb4ecf9d30c80473062e362560f81994c0030077). Two hypothetical family/education arrangements are linked by a question, with possible positive effects and coordination needs shown separately. The possible qualifier prevents unconditional causal claims; neither panel is dated or presented as a ranked household norm. Different adults participate in learning and care. At 360 px the school, varied learning/care scene, central consequence question and two large effect/coordination groups remain distinguishable. Small slogans and sublabels are not compulsory. At 680 px the possible benefits and coordination categories and concrete education/care arrangements are legible. Learning participants face their shared books correctly, and caregivers face children and learning tools. No readable inverted notebook or board is being used."
    },
