      "aiReviewer": "OpenAI Codex economics_visual_memory_audit",
      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e2-twenty-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/4c7c7297-b4bb-56cd-bbfe-85d4cdb784e8/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:b27298e371044e229c5aa4dbdf0e227673ec5e1dfd8b20c25436bc8051be59a2). Two clearly distinct questions: inward financing flows from equity and outside capital versus which private/business assets may be exposed to liability. The large question-mark shield avoids incorrectly asserting that outside finance automatically protects private assets or that a particular legal form always grants limited liability. At 360 px both panels, financing arrows, two purses and question-mark shield are identifiable; the two-question distinction remains legible. Mug and workshop slogans are optional. At 680 px the equity/outside-capital labels and private/business asset labels are readable without dense case text. The owner faces the laptop screen hidden from the viewer; its visible logo is on the back. The open notebook is blank without actor-inverted text. The large panels are explanatory overlays rather than physical documents she is reading."
