      "aiApproved": "yes",
      "aiApprovedAssetSha256": "sha256:ea1274bc4ca784af91ff9aef2cf4d8379b2775a673ce46c1a8c82cfb2ffcf496",
      "aiReviewedAt": "2026-10-08",
      "aiReviewer": "OpenAI Codex economics_visual_memory_audit",
      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e2-twenty-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/1826fe19-4d06-5183-9b41-9121ae1cc219/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:d4606bdf9455e3c1e21185ee1542d1a5bf87669d132d87efa263f91c2442c41a). Three examples match the current goal: a closed backpack with uncertain buyer and seller thought cutaway for information asymmetry; one flood-warning signal heard by several neighbors for a non-rival, non-excludable warning in this model; and one visible bicycle supplier with a barrier blocking a new shop for monopoly entry problems. No image claims that every shared physical good is public or every lone supplier is inefficient. At 360 px all three headings and the uncertain buyer, shared warning, existing shop and closed entry barrier remain recognizable. Warning wave/bell and forbidden new-shop icon carry meaning without the small sign text. At 680 px the thought bubble originates by the seller while the buyer has a separate question, and the public warning is clearly a signal rather than rival bottled water. The entry barrier is explicit. The buyer looks toward the closed backpack; no hidden product information is falsely shown as a page they can read. Neighbors face the public signal; shoppers and entry sign face the market scene appropriately."
    },
