      "aiApprovedAssetSha256": "sha256:aae05e1b278b41e6cd8832e017d946a29ef5d11627eaaac32fdd4d9adb662e6a",
      "aiReviewedAt": "2026-10-08",
      "aiReviewer": "OpenAI Codex economics_visual_memory_audit",
      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e1-seventeen-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/3ac589b5-f8a5-5192-b81d-ed94cde4177a/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:1baeb72d3c62311c9ed2804c8ec8919330c4b70530d39f314b3be418dd796679). Technical work, teaching and fatherly care are equally dignified activities beside an open opportunity doorway, balanced person symbols and policy discussion. These are possible roles and a stated equality aspiration rather than pink/blue segregation or proof equality has already been achieved. At 360 px the three activity headings, actors, open doorway and equality scale remain recognizable. The policy discussion is supplementary but visible. At 680 px care by a father and the common equality aspiration are clear; no historical before/after timeline is implied. The technical actor works toward the component and tools; the teacher addresses students with the book held appropriately; the father faces his child. The laptop back faces the audience and its users face the screen."
    },
