      "aiReviewedAt": "2026-10-08",
      "aiReviewer": "OpenAI Codex economics_visual_memory_audit",
      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e2-twenty-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/c4f27b51-958c-5416-a2de-d96a6e59e8b5/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:b6622ecbd2c21bf324bc09e4cf73c7b85e6cc4584332c7580e9ff5f6dc7b7f22). An owner and a bank are both capital providers with inward funding arrows, while a large question asks who bears risk and compares private/business asset symbols. It correctly avoids equating funding source with a predetermined liability allocation or promising that lenders never bear loss. At 360 px both providers, coin flows, workshop, two asset symbols and risk question remain clear. Decorative workshop signs are unnecessary. At 680 px the owner/bank distinction and the unresolved risk balance are easily read without small legal case text. The bank representative holds a closed BANK folder with a public identifying cover, not an actor-inverted page. No notebook or measurement device is being read."
