      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e2-twenty-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/4d578b42-8dac-5381-9836-9d7199451c74/correction-v2/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:10a7625b5b65e6a79237d600a94d7aa49e1b9d325a7cb563f45db9baf28325e3). The corrected left stage shows a helmeted actor actively riding a complete bicycle under Nutzen, resolving the manufacturing/use confusion. The right stage is now labelled Recycling and visibly sorts recovered materials/parts with recycling marks and a separate residual waste branch, resolving the earlier reuse/recycling ambiguity. Correctly directed large arrows connect use, repair and recycling; no perfect lossless recycling claim is made. At 360 px actual cycling, repair work, material sorting, all three headings and the circular arrows are recognizable. The residual waste icon remains separate. At 680 px the complete used bicycle and the recycling sorting bins are clear; the changed labels correspond to the actual scenes. The rider looks along their direction of travel and holds the bicycle handlebars normally. Repair and material work face the actors correctly; no legible reversed instrument or notebook appears."
