      "aiReviewer": "OpenAI Codex economics_visual_memory_audit",
      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e2-twenty-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/625b61ec-8561-5179-b59e-d3742b19c0e2/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:17ebbc17d990b78feb0dc9ca86db132129e0374822e1bb32428a08fd15c9711f). Three distinct instrument families: payment toward a public institution, trading certificates with opposing certificate/payment arrows beneath a schematic shared cap, and enforceable rules/checks. The comparison invitation does not assert that one instrument always works best or invent current rates and legal scope. At 360 px panel headings, tax/public-payment icon, two certificate traders with arrows, and regulatory checklist are visible. The footer comparison question remains legible without smaller legal detail. At 680 px the reverse directions of certificate and payment trade are clear and the cap remains a conceptual line rather than an invented scale. The rules worker demonstrates a clipboard toward the audience; he is not shown reading its back. The certificate is displayed between the two traders and no fine directional writing is falsely oriented."
