      "aiReviewer": "OpenAI Codex economics_visual_memory_audit",
      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e2-twenty-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/e7fbbb64-9f10-5d5d-8946-710aedc6794a/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:1804dc00395a6797685507ce92bd7dc1ddf05e6fd42ae581c9a93c619e968392). Owner funds flow toward the workshop as Eigenkapital; lender credit flows into the workshop and a separate smaller coin arrow returns to the lender. This distinguishes equity from debt without false rates or mandatory repayment of equity. The thoughtful owner and section-symbol shield introduce a liability question, not a universal guarantee of limited liability. At 360 px owner, lender, workshop, both funding labels and opposite-direction credit/return arrows are recognizable. Promotional shop signs are decorative; the liability symbol remains large. At 680 px the arrows and holding of coins are clear, and workshop ownership/financing is easy to distinguish from purchasing a bicycle. No actor reads an audience-facing notebook. The workshop signs address passers-by; the lender holds a closed folder and the owner contemplates the legal symbol."
