      "aiReviewedAt": "2026-10-08",
      "aiReviewer": "OpenAI Codex economics_visual_memory_audit",
      "aiNotes": "Actual independent image review: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-visualization-review/wirtschaft-e2-twenty-image-author-20261008-v1/independent-review/84955a75-16b7-50c1-9257-7054d813cd2f/independent-image-review.receipt.json (sha256:04d5c764f3b16a0c7d4077be56efa9939c8d7fea6b4b5a51d5902c7850bfb9a2). A planned backpack choice is contrasted with a salient sale sign and another product, inviting analysis of framing/salience in consumer choice. No false discount rate, product utility or compulsory purchasing decision is stated; the learner is thoughtful rather than portrayed as inevitably irrational. At 360 px planned backpack, competing products, sale cue and thought question remain distinct; only large labels are used. At 680 px the shopper gaze and dotted attention arrow align with the prominent action label, explaining the intended behavioral decision prompt. The shopper gazes at the offer rather than reading the audience-facing reference card; the card displays a picture without directional writing. The sale sign correctly faces shoppers."
